  <title>Miscellaneous revenue</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Miscellaneous revenue</gui></guiseq>
  records income that no invoice covers, such as a rebate, a refund or a sale
  of equipment.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the contact it came from. <gui>Contacts</gui> opens the
    contacts window.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Amount</gui>, choose the <gui>Date</gui> and add a
    <gui>Comment</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose how it was paid: a check number, a transfer to an account,
    or cash, as in <link xref="customer_payment"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Split it over revenue accounts: click <gui>Add row</gui>, double
    click a <gui>Revenue Account</gui> and type the row's <gui>Amount</gui>.
    <gui>Equalize</gui> splits the amount evenly; right click a row and choose
    <gui>Balance this row</gui> to give it what the others leave. <gui>Delete
    row</gui> removes one.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Post revenue</gui>, or <gui>Post revenue &amp; clear
    entries</gui> to enter another.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Until it can be posted, a message says what is missing, for instance
  <gui>Amount does not match total</gui>. A check or cash payment then waits
  in <link xref="deposits"/>.</p>

</page>
